cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use FastForest in your work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "FastForest: random-forest feature reduction for high-dimensional tabular data"
version: 1.0.0.dev0
date-released: "2026-10-12"
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/ThieleLab/streamlit_random_forest_analysis"
url: "https://fastforest.vmh.life"
abstract: >-
  FastForest trains a random forest on all features of a labelled table, searches for the
  smallest importance-ranked feature subset whose validation metrics stay within a bound of the
  full model, removes redundant features by Spearman-correlation clustering, and reports the final
  model on a held-out test split. It ships as a Python library, a command-line tool and a
  Streamlit web application.
authors:
  - family-names: Hulshof
    given-names: Tim O.
    affiliation: "School of Medicine and Ryan Institute, University of Galway, Ireland"
keywords:
  - random forest
  - feature selection
  - feature reduction
  - tabular data
  - metabolic modelling
